# How to Start This Project

## 1. Open the project folder

```powershell
cd "C:\Users\APPLE\Documents\Project\E-Commerce website"
```

## 2. Create environment files

```powershell
Copy-Item .env.example .env
Copy-Item .env server\.env -Force
```

Open `.env` and `server/.env`, then set these values:

```env
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DATABASE"
JWT_SECRET="change-this-to-a-long-secret"
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET="change-this-to-another-long-secret"
ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD="your-secure-admin-password"
PORT=4000
CLIENT_URL="http://localhost:5173"
UPLOAD_DIRECTORY="uploads"
```

For a simple hosted database, use Neon, Supabase, Railway, Render, or Aiven. If the provider gives an SSL connection string, use it exactly, usually with `?sslmode=require`.

## 3. Install dependencies

```powershell
npm install
```

## 4. Prepare the database

Your PostgreSQL database must already exist and be reachable from `DATABASE_URL`.

Generate Prisma client:

```powershell
npx prisma generate --schema server/prisma/schema.prisma
```

Run migrations:

```powershell
npm run prisma:migrate --workspace server
```

Seed demo data:

```powershell
npm run seed
```

Seeded admin account:

```text
Email: admin@example.com
Password: the ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD value from your .env file
```

## 5. Start both frontend and backend

```powershell
npm run dev
```

Then open:

```text
Customer website: http://localhost:5173
Admin dashboard:  http://localhost:5173/admin
Backend API:       http://localhost:4000
API docs:          http://localhost:4000/api/docs
```

## Start Server Only

```powershell
npm run dev --workspace server
```

## Start Client Only

```powershell
npm run dev --workspace client
```

## Useful Checks

TypeScript check:

```powershell
npm run typecheck
```

Production build:

```powershell
npm run build
```

Prisma Studio:

```powershell
npx prisma studio --schema server/prisma/schema.prisma
```

## Common Windows Note

If PowerShell blocks `npm`, use `npm` instead:

```powershell
npm install
npm run dev
```

## Prisma DATABASE_URL Fix

If Prisma says `DATABASE_URL` is missing, copy the root env file into the server folder:

```powershell
Copy-Item .env server\.env -Force
```

